P.O. Box 329 6802 Rivera T. 091 936 10 30 info@monteceneri.ch NOTICE OF COMPETITION FOR the RECRUITMENT OF INTERNS The Municipality of Monteceneri announces that the public competition for recruitment is open, starting from the school year 2027/2028, at the Municipal Administration of one: intern 52 weeks for obtaining the AFC with commercial professional maturity (Public Administration branch) The candidate we are looking for must comply with the following requirements.

1.1 Formal requirements

- swiss citizenship or other foreign nationality with residence permit, subject to agreements

internazionali;

- impeccable and uncensored conduct;

- healthy physical constitution suitable for the function and psycho-physical balance;

- passing the exams scheduled for the third school year;

- good academic results;

- dynamism, flexibility, spirit of initiative, willingness to learn and sense of responsibility;

- italian mother tongue and knowledge of national languages.

Working Condition:

- the salary is fr. 1,500 per month (+ 13th monthly payment);

- workplace: Bironico;

- at the end of the internship, the job employed by the Municipality will not be guaranteed.

Items to be supplied

- accompanying letter;

- curriculum vitae with recent photograph;

- SCHOOL REPORTS

- any internship certificates.

Any additional documentation may be requested later (e.g. criminal record and self-certification of health status).

Submission of applications

- applications accompanied by the required documents must reach the e-mail

concorsi@monteceneri.ch or in a closed envelope, with the external wording "52-week internship contest" at the Municipal Chancellery, P.O. Box 329, 6802 Rivera, by Monday, November 30, 2026 at 12:00. The Municipality reserves the right not to proceed with the recruitment in the absence of candidates deemed suitable for the function. The Council of State is given the right to appeal against this notice within 30 days of its publication. The MUNICIPALITY OF Monteceneri, 27 October 2026 Municipality of Monteceneri

